# Replay places a tube at its first full record even if that job was deleted later: job 2 creates a before job 3 creates b, and deleting job 2 does not free a (job 4 holds it), so the list is default, b, a before the restart and default, a, b after it.
!binlog
@a send "use b\r\n"
@a recv
@b send "put 0 0 60 1\r\n1\r\n"
@b recv
@c send "use a\r\n"
@c recv
@c send "put 0 0 60 1\r\n2\r\n"
@c recv
@a send "put 0 0 60 1\r\n3\r\n"
@a recv
@c send "put 0 0 60 1\r\n4\r\n"
@c recv
@a send "delete 2\r\n"
@a recv
@a send "list-tubes\r\n"
@a recv
crash
@a send "list-tubes\r\n"
@a recv
restart
@a send "list-tubes\r\n"
@a recv
@a send "stats-tube a\r\n"
@a recv
